robots.txt is not in git.

Its contents depend on which host this installation answers as: only the hosts
listed in `seo.robots.public_hosts` are served a policy that permits indexing,
and every other host is served `Disallow: /`. A single committed file could
only ever be right for one of them.

It is written at deploy time by:

    php artisan seo:publish-robots

That command belongs in the deployment script of every environment, after
`composer install`. Until it has run on a host, `/robots.txt` is answered by
the route in routes/web.php, which serves the identical body — slower, but
never a 404, which a crawler reads as "no rules at all".

Edit config/seo.php to change the policy, never this directory.
